		<a name="msg16178"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=519" title="View the profile of Darcc">Darcc</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 2<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								An Everquest Player on Rodcet Nife<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=519"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1492.msg16178#msg16178"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1492.msg16178#msg16178">Re: Dang Fabled and being KSed</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #34 on:</b> April 03, 2005, 03:27:11 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Ks&#039;ed is such a vague term nowadays.  I had always viewed it as *if the mobs health is below 99% and its biteing something, it&#039;s engaged*.   Maybe thats just what I&#039;ve learned from being in Raid guilds, when your whole guild is set up and before an arrow is fired, 80 members of Forsaken zerg your target and you look like your sitting on your thumb.<br /><br />Was that a KS?  Did Forsaken take my mob, because I was rightfully stareing at it?  Sure, I was pissed, but they were mobile and ready for the takedown.....my guild lost, they won.  Boo hoo, it WILL spawn again.<br /><br />Fabled&#039;s I understand are a different story.  They may not be here again (least not for a year) and there are so many things people want.  But quite frankly, it&#039;s the way its always been.  Whether it be Fabled, PoP gods, the named in BoT (named in any zone for that matter), desired targets are highly contested.  Deal.<br /><br />Just today my friend asked me to come kill Lodi for him, I say sure.  Run out to Iceclad to find a lvl 40 ranger trying to keep it occupied while his Necro friend runs there from GD.  He figured it was engaged......from what I understand, it wasn&#039;t.  It was Aggroed, not engaged.  I even asked him if he was going to fight it, or sit there and run around for the next hour.<br /><br />So.......I nuked it.  (monk Nuke rules), apparently the small ranger had thouroughly pissed off Lodi and when he dropped below 95% it summoned him and ate him.  That...I felt bad for, but for about 5 seconds.  Who is the bigger dick?  Me for takeing the aggroed Lodi that the ranger couldnt handle?  Or the Ranger for trying to tell me tough shit it&#039;s his when he dosent have the force to take it down readily available?<br /><br />Lodi dies, my friend gets his loot and I walk away.  From the posts, it sounds almost like the same thing, something may have been aggroed, but it wasn&#039;t engaged if it took off after another group.  It was even admitted that the &#039;campers&#039; already had their hands full with a train, but it was decided they had better get the mob in camp.  That mob was derailed, which means it wasnt engaged, which means it isn&#039;t kill stealing.<br /><br />Atleast thats my understanding, and what the many unique players in this game have taught me throughout my travels.  I have walked over a groups corpses to kill a mob 20 levels lower than me just to grab something for my twink and they called me an asshole for not respecting their camp.....conviniently being camped by their corpses, they must&#039;ve been there in spirit, because I wronged someone, somehow.<br /><br />If you find my understanding of &#039;Ks&#039;ing&#039; to be wrong, then mildly expand your reality for a moment and remember your not the only one trying to better himself or his friends in this game.  Not everyone will think like you, respect is not something which you can expect to be given by other players.  <br /><br />On a side note, I find Kin&#039;s post about farming Qvic absolutely hillarious.  MAinly because everytime I chat with him I still remember the funniest moment I ever spent with him, as a baby ranger in paludals frantically trying to cure himself of Phlarg cooties, succumbing too it 10 minutes later when he finally ran out of mana.  Good news Kin!!  That Dot ain&#039;t so bad now, so the newbies will never have to go through the pain you suffered  <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/cool.gif" alt="Cool" border="0" /><br /><br />Anyways......I should really stay away from message boards when I&#039;m drunk.  <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/devil1.gif" alt="Devil" border="0" /><br /><br />Laterzz~~
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Darcc
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg16181"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=765" title="View the profile of Moraganna">Moraganna</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Female.gif" alt="Female" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 129<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/ceres.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Kiss muh cute ass~<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=765"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1492.msg16181#msg16181"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1492.msg16181#msg16181">Re: Dang Fabled and being KSed</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #35 on:</b> April 03, 2005, 10:17:36 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Actually any mob that is engaged, being pulled or actually mellee engaged is concidered a ks if anyone takes the mob after one of those things have been done, however, you can not train a mob around by keeping it agro for a long period of time and expect others to respect this rule. Even a GM would concider you silly if you tried to claim you where camping a mob just because you had agro on it. The mob does not have to be below 100% health just agro on another player, reguardless if that player can take out the mob or not that is the rule of KSing. <br /><br />I normally will ask politely and give them a time limit *fair time limit of coarse.* I do not expect to sit there and wait on other players to gather their forces while my force sits on the side lines and waits. Of coarse you do have those people who refuse to use the *play nice rules* and becomes enraged that you would even concider taking their mob that they have been kiting for 10+ minutes so their crew could get there and kill it for them to get the loot. Those people I tend to forget the *play nice rules* for. 
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><div align="center"><br /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=847985" target="_blank"> <img src="http://home.mindspring.com/~jkocie/bb.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a> <br /><br />BUFF BISH<br />Moraganna Macabre<br />&quot;I don&#039;t know the the key to success, but the key to failure is trying to please everbody&quot;</div>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
