	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg16189"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=961" title="View the profile of AverseThule">AverseThule</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 27<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/evildude.jpg" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								&lt;Oggok Foreign Legion&gt;<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=961"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1492.msg16189#msg16189"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1492.msg16189#msg16189">Re: Dang Fabled and being KSed</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #37 on:</b> April 03, 2005, 02:40:56 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1492.msg16096#msg16096">Quote from: Kkhaarn on April 01, 2005, 02:08:02 am</a></div><div class="quote">whats with this fucking list shit? where did this come from?<br /><br />i had a full group of guildies in there the other day and people were like whats the list like?  whats this list you speak of? im killing til everyone in my group gets one that wants one and leaving.<br /><br />i guess some people zone in alone and expect to get on a list so that someone will kill the mob for them.<br /><br />and yes you can camp everything if you can clear everything. you slack on clearing and its could become no longer yours.<br /><br />i have farmed most of the fabled thats worth a shit and KC is the only place i have seen with people calling list checks.<br /></div><br />Lists date back to the beginning of EQ.&nbsp; I used to be on a &#039;list&#039; for Lguk guise, Najena Jboots, some headpiece in permafrost (runed circlet?), BIBS, some +3 str ring in Blackburrow(!), etc...&nbsp; Heck, just about any worthwhile piece of loot I ended up joining a camp in progress and put at the end of a list.<br /><br />Fabled tend to bring out more difficult situtations because the other mobs in the zone, relative to them, are so weak.&nbsp; If the zone was entirely beefed up, even the non fabled, then &quot;claiming&quot; an entire zone would be much more difficult.<br /><br />I remember when ppl were getting too tough for zones and &quot;farming&quot; multiple camps the general rule seemed to be that you could claim more than one camp room but if another group came into one of the additional rooms then you pretty much lost rights to that particular room since they were wiling to sit their force in that actual room and wait for the named.&nbsp; This gave you rights to one named room as your &quot;priority&quot; camp and then you could pull other named camps if no one was on them, but once someone came to those rooms you lost your rights.&nbsp; Maybe this wasnt everyone&#039;s experience on the server, but it was pretty consistent with what I saw.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
