	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg16332"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=202" title="View the profile of xaanru">xaanru</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 116<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								I&#039;m not a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=202"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1492.msg16332#msg16332"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1492.msg16332#msg16332">Re: Dang Fabled and being KSed</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #42 on:</b> April 10, 2005, 07:37:47 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">the general rule seemed to be that you could claim more than one camp room but if another group came into one of the additional rooms then you pretty much lost rights to that particular room since they were wiling to sit their force in that actual room and wait for the named.&nbsp; This gave you rights to one named room as your &quot;priority&quot; camp and then you could pull other named camps if no one was on them, but once someone came to those rooms you lost your rights.&nbsp; Maybe this wasnt everyone&#039;s experience on the server, but it was pretty consistent with what I saw. </div><br />Yep, thats pretty much the way i always understood it as well. A good example back in the day was highkeep. You could hold the warrior and raider rooms both, if nobody were in the other, but if another group showed, you had to pick one. Or more recently, the cubby/hill camps in WoS.<br /><br />I always thought it was funny that one group would often try to have two different members call both camps, to try to fool people into thinking both were camped.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg16340"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=420" title="View the profile of Tiiden">Tiiden</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Guild Officer<br />
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 130<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.convictioneq.com/images/beware.gif" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								The Last of the Magicians!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=420"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1492.msg16340#msg16340"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1492.msg16340#msg16340">Re: Dang Fabled and being KSed</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #43 on:</b> April 10, 2005, 05:30:27 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1492.msg16181#msg16181">Quote from: Moraganna on April 03, 2005, 10:17:36 am</a></div><div class="quote">Actually any mob that is engaged, being pulled or actually mellee engaged is concidered a ks if anyone takes the mob after one of those things have been done, however, you can not train a mob around by keeping it agro for a long period of time and expect others to respect this rule. <br /></div><br />You&#039;re on the right track, but incorrect.&nbsp; The actual rule enforced by the GMs, is that one must be first on the target&#039;s agro list WITH sufficient force to kill in order to have claim to the target.&nbsp; If you do not have sufficient force to kill at the time of engaging, you have no claim to the target, and anyone with sufficient force may take agro and kill the mob, legally.&nbsp; <br /><br />We saw this enforced many times back in Velious when it took a small raid to kill Lodizal, and druids would always kite it around while their guild&#039;s raid force got ported in, and they whined and cried when another guild got there first and snatched it from them, only to see the GMs say, &quot;Sorry, that&#039;s fair.&quot;<br /><br />Straight from the source: <a href="http://eqlive.station.sony.com/support/customer_service/cs_rules_of_conduct.jsp" target="_blank">http://eqlive.station.sony.com/support/customer_service/cs_rules_of_conduct.jsp</a><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">Kill Stealing is defined as the killing of an NPC for any reason that is already fighting or pursuing another player or group that is <b>prepared to engage</b> that same NPC without that group&#039;s specific permission.</div>
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=370607" target="_blank">http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=370607</a><br />70 Magician, retired.
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg16341"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=765" title="View the profile of Moraganna">Moraganna</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Female.gif" alt="Female" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 129<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/ceres.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Kiss muh cute ass~<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=765"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1492.msg16341#msg16341"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1492.msg16341#msg16341">Re: Dang Fabled and being KSed</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #44 on:</b> April 10, 2005, 08:31:01 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Sorry Tiiden you are incorrect, <br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">1. You may not steal kills.<br /><br />Kill Stealing is defined as the killing of an NPC for any reason that is <i>already fighting <span style="text-decoration: underline;"><b>or</b></span> pursuing another player <span style="text-decoration: underline;"><b>or</b></span> group that is prepared to engage </i> that same NPC without that group&#039;s specific permission.<br /><br />The intent of this rule is discourage and make note of habitual Kill Stealers, not to punish those who honestly try to work together or those who make an honest mistake. Its enforcement by the EverQuest Customer Service Staff will reflect this philosophy.</div>
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									&#171; <i>Last Edit: April 10, 2005, 08:35:58 pm by Moraganna</i> &#187;
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><div align="center"><br /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=847985" target="_blank"> <img src="http://home.mindspring.com/~jkocie/bb.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a> <br /><br />BUFF BISH<br />Moraganna Macabre<br />&quot;I don&#039;t know the the key to success, but the key to failure is trying to please everbody&quot;</div>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
